  "github_release": {
    "id": 444175813,
    "tag_name": "v0.4.0",
    "name": "rust-mirror 0.4.0",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/rustcommons/rust-mirror/releases/tag/v0.4.0",
    "published_at": "2026-11-13T11:59:42Z",
    "body": "# rust-mirror 0.4.0\n\n## Changes\n\n- Mirror an organization-wide curated crate catalog with Cargo registry-dependency\n  syntax, aliases, declared features, latest-N rules and exact pins.\n- Resolve bounded native dependency closures without a Cargo binary at runtime.\n  Preview counts, optional HEAD size estimates, budgets and inclusion explanations;\n  approve the whole frozen plan before archive downloads.\n- Fetch with bounded concurrency, retry notices, cancellation, resumable state and\n  index-checksum verification. Emit an immutable static sparse registry with\n  byte-preserved index lines and generation-local archive URLs.\n- Retain older mirrored versions and protect crate generations during explicit\n  whole-generation pruning. Publish schema 4 using the existing no-overwrite,\n  preflight and marker-last rules.\n- Expose catalog editing/paste diagnostics, preview/discovery/client-config APIs\n  and additive protocol-1 completion, file-count and typed retry events.\n\n## Upgrade\n\nRust/Cargo 1.90+ remains required. Existing toolchain inventory schemas 1/2/3 and\ncommands remain supported. Crate inventory schema 4 requires this version; older\nreaders refuse it. Frozen crate plans use their own schema 1. Protocol 1 remains\nadditive; Rust consumers matching public event variants exhaustively or constructing\nexpanded report structs may need updates. Use crate-aware retention for crate\nleaves; toolchain pruning refuses them.\n\nDirect `semver` and `serde_json` dependencies were owner-approved during native\ncrate design; they are new relative to published 0.3.0. No Cargo library, external\nruntime Cargo, third-party solver or direct tar/flate2 dependency is introduced.\nA fresh generation needs its eventual immutable HTTPS base URL before planning.\nConfigure Cargo source replacement explicitly; publication does not activate routing.\n\n## Validation and limits\n\nThe [Phase 1 record](https://github.com/rustcommons/rust-mirror/blob/main/docs/evals/2026-11-13-crates-mvp.md)\nidentifies the qualified source and CI. The dated 100-root corpus had no exclusions:\n186 native versions matched the Cargo lockfile union, with 45,125,358 archive bytes\non each side and 0% measured byte overfetch. Planning downloaded no archives.\nThese measurements describe that corpus, not all future catalogs.\n\nIsolated HTTPS Cargo fetch/build/offline client checks ran on Linux, Windows and\nmacOS, building **itoa**, not all 100 crates or arbitrary foreign targets. Kill,\nstdin-cancel and range-resume checks used a separate synthetic payload. Actual\ndisposable Nexus Raw schema-4 publication and Cargo consumption were proved on\n**Linux only**, using a recorded legacy OSS test instance behind a verified TLS\nproxy. This is neither production Nexus qualification nor a recommended server version.\nUnchanged Phase 1 runtime evidence carries into this release candidate; release\npackage/install checks are recorded separately before merge.\n\nHistorical cohorts preserve their original index bytes and independent proofs.\nThe combined served index is replayed against historical/current profiles; if it\nneeds an unmirrored edge or exceeds resource bounds, planning **refuses** rather\nthan exposing an incomplete generation. This conservative refusal is an MVP limit.\nDev dependencies are excluded; enabled features, bounded profiles and all-platform\nnormal/build dependencies govern closure. No arbitrary Cargo completeness guarantee\nor runtime build-safety/license/security review is implied by checksum verification.\n\nCargo.lock import, private/alternate registries, scheduling, in-generation compaction,\nremote pruning and GUI work remain deferred. Upstream signatures are preserved,\nnot independently verified. Publication is owner-authorized; the coordinator merges\nand uploads the qualified candidate before postpublication verification.\n\n## Links\n\n- [Source tag](https://github.com/rustcommons/rust-mirror/tree/v0.4.0)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/rustcommons/rust-mirror/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Crate guide and client setup](https://github.com/rustcommons/rust-mirror/blob/main/docs/CRATES.md)\n- [User guide](https://github.com/rustcommons/rust-mirror/blob/main/docs/USER-GUIDE.md)\n- [Command reference](https://github.com/rustcommons/rust-mirror/blob/main/docs/CLI-REFERENCE.md)\n- [Protocol 1](https://github.com/rustcommons/rust-mirror/blob/main/docs/EVENTS.md)\n- [Release policy](https://github.com/rustcommons/rust-mirror/blob/main/docs/RELEASING.md)\n",
